# Ed25519 signing key for Certificate.signature (Module 12 — see
# docs/stages/12-certificates.md Section 5 and docs/DECISIONS.md D34).
# Read only by the api container — certificate rendering happens
# synchronously in the API's request thread, unlike GitHub token
# decryption, so the worker never needs this value.
#
# Copy this file to certificate_signing_key.txt (gitignored) and fill
# in a real key. A plain `openssl rand -hex 32` does NOT produce a
# valid Ed25519 key — generate one with:
#   pnpm --filter @raptor/api exec ts-node -T \
#     src/scripts/generate-certificate-signing-key.ts
#
# Rotating this value makes every previously-issued certificate's
# signature unverifiable against the new key (this platform has no key
# -rotation registry yet — see CertificateSigningService's own comment).
change-me-to-a-hex-encoded-ed25519-pkcs8-key
